        <body>
            <div xml:id="d381">

                <pb facs="0466" n="362" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg362"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4236: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland (Wilson) to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-16T20:00:00+01:00">February 16, 1932—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 16—5:21 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>24. Following is memorandum from Sweetser of private meeting of Twelve this
                    afternoon: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Twelve approved this afternoon the text of the communication to be
                            made to Japan. That text was given to Mr. Sato this evening with
                            covering letter from Boncour as President of the Council for
                            transmission to Tokyo. It will be published here probably tomorrow
                            morning subject to any desire expressed by the Japanese.</p>
                        <p>This is the first communication that the Council has made to one party
                            only in the dispute. The only change of substance introduced this
                            afternoon was the inclusion of a reference to the Nine-Power Treaty
                            suggested by the British.”</p></quote></p>
                <p>See my 25, February 16, 9 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
